# assets#18: a deposit that would push available+locked past Long.MAX_VALUE is REJECTED and mutates
# nothing.
#
# Before the fix it wrapped the balance NEGATIVE, silently: no exception, no fault event, no log line,
# and the conservation checks still passed because the wrapped value was internally consistent. The
# account then reported no funds and every subsequent hold on that asset was rejected
# INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS. It was found by a benchmark that pre-funded the same accounts twice.
#
# Two things in the golden below carry the assertion:
#   1. the second DEPOSIT emits NOTHING (a rejected deposit has no ack message and no balance line),
#   2. the HOLD after it is ACCEPTED, which is only possible if the balance is still positive.
CLOCK 1000
DEPOSIT u=1 asset=0 amt=92233720368.0
DEPOSIT u=1 asset=0 amt=92233720368.0
HOLD u=1 order=1 asset=0 amt=1000.0
RELEASE order=1 u=1
